Berkshire Hathaway Warren Buffett disclosed the changes in the portfolio in the first quarter of 2018 Invest Academy Posted On May 16, 2018 Share On Facebook UNITED STATES – Major changes in the investment portfolio of Berkshire Hathaway: Q1 2018 vs. Q4 2017:
Increased positions: AAPL (up to ~ 239.57 million shares from ~ 165.33 million shares), TEVA (up ~ 40.54 million shares from ~ 18.88 million shares), MON (up to ~ 18.97 million shares with ~ 11.71 million shares) ;
Saved positions: BAC (~ 679 million shares), WFC (~ 456.51 million shares), KO (~ 400 million shares), KHC (~ 325.63 million shares), AXP (~ 151.61 million shares);
Abolished positions: IBM (with ~ 2.05 million shares), GHC (with ~ 0.11 million shares);
Abbreviated positions: PSX (up to ~ 45.69 million shares with ~ 80.69 million shares), VRSK (up ~ 0.28 million shares with ~ 1.56 million shares). 0
